                <pb facs="0086" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/470: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Tunis</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Springs</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tunis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-28T23:00:00+01:00">September 28, 1938—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 28—9:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s September 27, 4 p.m. Tunisia will give her support to France in the
                    event of a general war in Europe. There is great uneasiness due to the absence
                    of adequate protection against gas. In the event that Italy should oppose France
                    the protection of American born children of Italian parents will be a
                    problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Springs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
